# Resolved by `op run` whenever the podcast talks to X: the check, posts,
# media uploads, the metrics reads. Committed on purpose: every op:// below
# is a REFERENCE, not a value.
#
#   op run --env-file=tools/x.env -- ./tools/x.py check
#
# Two API Credential items for the app `podcast-engine` in the X Developer
# Console, so the fields are username + credential. X hands out two kinds of
# user credential and `./tools/x.py check` tells them apart:
#   OAuth 1.0a: the app item holds the API Key and Secret; the token item the
#               Access Token and Secret generated in the console for the
#               show's account. Neither expires nor rotates.
#   OAuth 2.0:  the app item holds the Client ID and Client Secret; the token
#               item the account id and the refresh token `./tools/x.py auth`
#               printed once. X retires a refresh token on use and returns a
#               new one, so the item is the live copy: whatever refreshes it
#               writes the new token back to the same field first.
X_APP_ID=op://Engineering/X podcast app/username
X_APP_SECRET=op://Engineering/X podcast app/credential
X_TOKEN=op://Engineering/X podcast token/username
X_TOKEN_SECRET=op://Engineering/X podcast token/credential
